or bridge-topics can be used to link dif- ferent pieces of evidence from which a multi-hop query’s answer is derived."},{"id":"c3","chunkId":"743155d9b0541c99_c_b634db6727fa46c3","docId":"743155d9b0541c99","docTitle":"2401.15391_MultiHop_RAG_Benchmarking_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Multi_Hop","page":11,"quote":"<News> <evidence> Table 7: Claim Generation Prompting A multi-hop question is a query requiring multiple inferential leaps or accessing several pieces of information from different locations or sources to arrive at an answer."},{"id":"c4","chunkId":"743155d9b0541c99_c_6b9454acd0180e9a","docId":"743155d9b0541c99","docTitle":"2401.15391_MultiHop_RAG_Benchmarking_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Multi_Hop","page":1,"quote":"However, we find that existing RAG sys- tems are inadequate in answering multi-hop queries, which require retrieving and reasoning over multiple pieces of supporting evidence."},{"id":"c5","chunkId":"743155d9b0541c99_c_43f9b3c00e35000e","docId":"743155d9b0541c99","docTitle":"2401.15391_MultiHop_RAG_Benchmarking_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Multi_Hop","page":1,"quote":"n necessi- tates retrieving and reasoning over evidence from multiple documents, a process known as multi-hop query."},{"id":"c6","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_06dea6d333690cf5","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":15,"quote":"Evidence aggregation for answer re- ranking in open-domain question answering."},{"id":"c7","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_22b017c66dee135b","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":9,"quote":"Our approach does have several differences, including less of emphasis on lightly editing a retrieved item, but on aggregating content from several pieces of retrieved content, as well as learning latent retrieval, and retrieving evidence"},{"id":"c8","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_3af9b0854c8045f7","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":3,"quote":"3.2 Evidence Retrieval Here we evaluate chunkers at a finer granularity than the previous experiment by measuring their abilities to locate evidence sentences."},{"id":"c9","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_a97c6dcc5e5dcb61","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":5,"quote":"The task requires retrieving evidence from Wikipedia relating to the claim and then reasoning over this evidence to classify whether the claim is true, false, or unveriﬁable from Wikipedia alone."},{"id":"c10","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_5501d7fc1ea7a965","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":31,"quote":"[175] utilize the off-the-shelf MedCPT retriever, a tool specifically tailored for retrieving documents in response to biomedical queries, capable of retrieving up to ten relevant pieces of evidence for each input."},{"id":"c11","chunkId":"743155d9b0541c99_c_6b9454acd0180e9a","docId":"743155d9b0541c99","docTitle":"2401.15391_MultiHop_RAG_Benchmarking_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Multi_Hop","page":1,"quote":"In this paper, we develop a novel dataset, MultiHop-RAG, which consists of a knowledge base, a large collection of multi- hop queries, their ground-truth answers, and the associated supporting evidence."},{"id":"c12","chunkId":"743155d9b0541c99_c_8faf205d52225055","docId":"743155d9b0541c99","docTitle":"2401.15391_MultiHop_RAG_Benchmarking_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Multi_Hop","page":2,"quote":"including supporting evidence from two news articles, the paraphrased claim, the bridge-topic and bridge-entity, and the corresponding answer."},{"id":"c13","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_6ac97909cee2f6ae","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":7,"quote":"RAG achieves an accuracy within 2.7% of this model, despite being supplied with only the claim and retrieving its own evidence."},{"id":"c14","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_181c8bf27b0b14b3","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":3,"quote":"Instead, each retrieved chunk is mapped back to either the source document or the included evidence sentences."},{"id":"c15","chunkId":"d9eaa1398abac0df_c_9f9f8e3c98bd1183","docId":"d9eaa1398abac0df","docTitle":"2310.11511_Self_RAG_Learning_to_Retrieve_Generate_and_Critique_through_Self_Refle","page":25,"quote":"[No] Explanation This instruction asks us to write a short story, which does not require external evidence to verify."},{"id":"c16","chunkId":"743155d9b0541c99_c_a191f5bcfece81a2","docId":"743155d9b0541c99","docTitle":"2401.15391_MultiHop_RAG_Benchmarking_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Multi_Hop","page":4,"quote":"However, the raw evidence obtained from Step 2 is not ideal for query generation due to inconsistency in linguistic structure."},{"id":"c17","chunkId":"d9eaa1398abac0df_c_82f86b5e225f537f","docId":"d9eaa1398abac0df","docTitle":"2310.11511_Self_RAG_Learning_to_Retrieve_Generate_and_Critique_through_Self_Refle","page":6,"quote":"For instance, to ensure that result y is mostly supported by evidence, we can set a weight term for the ISSUP score higher, while relatively lowering weights for other aspects."},{"id":"c18","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_b44143332fc03b52","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":4,"quote":"(v) SciFact retrieves evi- dence for claims verification."},{"id":"c19","chunkId":"23e3249e9a1e7541_c_4805baae415f96b7","docId":"23e3249e9a1e7541","docTitle":"2005.11401_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Knowledge_Intensive_NLP_Tasks","page":5,"quote":"MS-MARCO SotA is [4], FEVER-3 is [68] and FEVER-2 is [57] *Uses gold 